From: Vahiru <nekovahiru@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: gen1 解码器 drain 之后不 streamoff 也能接着解：EOS 时不自动 flush 输出口，START 时重置 LAST 状态（本地，#128 §15）

案卷 docs/stage4-findings.md #128 §14–§15。**本地补丁**。

现象（iris-k6 … k10，2026-09-28）：播到结尾（drain 完成）之后的**第一次 seek 没有输出**，再 seek 一次又好了；
AVC / HEVC / VP9 都一样，venus 同一测试 PASS。对应实际使用里"播完拖回开头重看"。

strace 对比（HAL android.hardware.media.c2-service-v4l2，同一个 `iris-seek-test seek:1:400`）：两边都是 STOP → 取回 LAST →
把那个空缓冲重新排回 → START；之后 v4l2_codec2 因为已经 Idle，seek 的 flush 在 V4L2 层什么都不做
（V4L2Decoder::flush() 开头 `if (mState == State::Idle) return;`），直接送新输入。venus 接着出帧；
iris 上新输入照样被吃掉（EBD 都回来），却一帧输出都没有，直到下一次真正 streamoff / streamon CAPTURE。

原因：`iris_hfi_gen1_session_ftb_done()` 收到带 EOS、长度 0 的输出缓冲时自动发 HFI_FLUSH_OUTPUT，
固件把 DPB（split 模式下 stream 0 的内部缓冲）全部退回；gen1 没有 session_resume_drain，
V4L2_DEC_CMD_START（iris_vdec_start_cmd）只清驱动里的状态位，谁也不把 DPB 再交给固件 ⇒ 固件没有参考帧缓冲可用。
k10 的 HFI 跟踪：EOS 那条 FLUSH_OUTPUT 之后退回一串 stream 0 的空缓冲，直到下一次 CAPTURE streamon 才又出现 6 条 stream 0 的 FTB。
venus 在 EOS 时不 flush（DPB 一直留在固件手里）。

修法：EOS 时不发这条 FLUSH_OUTPUT，只保留 drain_last 的状态处理。剩下的输出缓冲留在固件里：
客户端要么 START 后接着解（正是这里要的），要么 streamoff（那时 CAPTURE / OUTPUT streamoff 的 FLUSH_ALL 会把它们退回）。
顺带：这样除了分辨率切换那一处，gen1 解码器不再发 FLUSH_OUTPUT —— 正是它在收尾时让华为固件卡死过（0065）。
0644 模块参数 `qcom_iris.eos_flush`（默认 N；Y = 上游行为，用来 A/B）。

第二处（k11 上查出）：修掉第一处以后，"播完后 seek"通了，但**每隔一次 drain 就收不到 EOS**。
`inst->last_buffer_dequeued` 在交出 LAST 缓冲时置位，上游只在 streamon（iris_process_streamon_input / _output）时清；
drain 之后 v4l2_codec2 不再 streamoff / streamon ⇒ 下一次 drain 时 EOS 缓冲不会被标 LAST（`iris_hfi_gen1_session_ftb_done`
里 `!inst->last_buffer_dequeued` 的判断），HAL 等不到 LAST，drain 永远不完成。k11 用 v4l2 tracepoint 数：4 次 drain 只出了 2 个 LAST。
修法：`iris_vdec_start_cmd()` 离开 drain / DRC 状态时清 `last_buffer_dequeued`，并 `v4l2_m2m_clear_state()`
（LAST 时 `v4l2_m2m_mark_stopped()` 置上的"已停止"，上游从不清；v4l2_m2m_decoder_cmd() 在 START 时本来就会清）。
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_response.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_response.c
index bfd7495..314167f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_response.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_response.c
@@ -425,14 +425,23 @@ static void iris_hfi_gen1_session_ftb_done(struct iris_inst *inst, void *packet)
 	}
 
 	if ((hfi_flags & HFI_BUFFERFLAG_EOS) && !filled_len) {
-		reinit_completion(&inst->flush_completion);
-
-		flush_pkt.shdr.hdr.size = sizeof(struct hfi_session_flush_pkt);
-		flush_pkt.shdr.hdr.pkt_type = HFI_CMD_SESSION_FLUSH;
-		flush_pkt.shdr.session_id = inst->session_id;
-		flush_pkt.flush_type = HFI_FLUSH_OUTPUT;
-		if (!iris_hfi_queue_cmd_write(core, &flush_pkt, flush_pkt.shdr.hdr.size))
-			inst->flush_responses_pending++;
+		/*
+		 * gaokun3 0067 (#128 §15): upstream flushes the output port here. That hands
+		 * the DPBs back, and gen1 has nothing on V4L2_DEC_CMD_START that queues them
+		 * again, so a decode resumed after the drain (v4l2_codec2 does not stream off
+		 * for a seek once drained) gets input consumed but no output. venus does not
+		 * flush at EOS either.
+		 */
+		if (READ_ONCE(iris_eos_flush)) {
+			reinit_completion(&inst->flush_completion);
+
+			flush_pkt.shdr.hdr.size = sizeof(struct hfi_session_flush_pkt);
+			flush_pkt.shdr.hdr.pkt_type = HFI_CMD_SESSION_FLUSH;
+			flush_pkt.shdr.session_id = inst->session_id;
+			flush_pkt.flush_type = HFI_FLUSH_OUTPUT;
+			if (!iris_hfi_queue_cmd_write(core, &flush_pkt, flush_pkt.shdr.hdr.size))
+				inst->flush_responses_pending++;
+		}
 
 		iris_inst_sub_state_change_drain_last(inst);
 	}
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_instance.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_instance.h
index c157a01..71ed2ea 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_instance.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_instance.h
@@ -36,6 +36,8 @@ enum iris_fmt_type_cap {
  * then both streamon) is carried out; see iris_vdec.c.
  */
 extern unsigned int iris_seek_mode;
+/* gaokun3 0067: flush the output port when the EOS buffer comes back (upstream); see iris_vdec.c */
+extern bool iris_eos_flush;
 
 /**
  * struct iris_inst - holds per video instance parameters
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
index f25b7da..15e2164 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
@@ -378,6 +378,15 @@ unsigned int iris_seek_mode = 1;
 module_param_named(seek_mode, iris_seek_mode, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(seek_mode, "gaokun3: decoder seek (OUTPUT streamoff after CAPTURE streamoff): 1 flush and continue like venus (default), 0 upstream STOP + restart");
 
+/*
+ * gaokun3 0067 (#128 §15): Y = upstream, flush the output port when the EOS buffer comes
+ * back. That returns the DPBs and nothing queues them again on V4L2_DEC_CMD_START, so the
+ * first seek after the end of a stream decodes nothing.
+ */
+bool iris_eos_flush;
+module_param_named(eos_flush, iris_eos_flush, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(eos_flush, "gaokun3: flush the output port when the EOS buffer comes back (upstream); N keeps the DPBs with the firmware like venus so decoding can resume after a drain");
+
 int iris_vdec_streamon_input(struct iris_inst *inst)
 {
 	int ret;
@@ -561,6 +570,15 @@ int iris_vdec_start_cmd(struct iris_inst *inst)
 		return -EBUSY;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * gaokun3 0067 (#128 §15): decoding resumes here without a streamoff (v4l2_codec2
+	 * seeks after a drain without one), so the next drain must be able to mark its EOS
+	 * buffer LAST again. Upstream only resets this on streamon, and every second drain
+	 * then never completes. The m2m stopped state set with the LAST buffer goes too.
+	 */
+	inst->last_buffer_dequeued = false;
+	v4l2_m2m_clear_state(inst->m2m_ctx);
+
 	return iris_inst_change_sub_state(inst, clear_sub_state, 0);
 }
 
